+##### onRetry(context)
+
+Type: `Function`
+
+Callback invoked only when another attempt is going to happen, right before the wait. Receives the same context object as `onFailedAttempt`. Useful for retry metrics, since unlike `onFailedAttempt` it is not called for the final failure.
+
+The function is called _after_ `onFailedAttempt`, `shouldRetry`, and `shouldConsumeRetry`, so it is _not_ called when the error is thrown instead of retried: `AbortError`, an abort through `signal`, a `TypeError` (except network errors), `shouldRetry` returning `false`, or `retries` or `maxRetryTime` being exhausted. It is called when `shouldConsumeRetry` returns `false`, since the next attempt still happens, with a `retryDelay` of `0`.
+
+The function can return a promise, which is awaited before the wait starts, and the wait is not shortened by the time it takes.
+
+If the function throws, all retries will be aborted and the original promise will reject with the thrown error.
+
+```js
+import pRetry from 'p-retry';
+
+const run = async () => { … };
+
+const result = await pRetry(run, {
+	onRetry: ({error, attemptNumber}) => {
+		metrics.increment('retries', {reason: error.name, attemptNumber});
+	}
+});
+```
+
 ##### shouldRetry(context)
 
 Type: `Function`
